body:
This is a strong setup/runbook signal, especially for non-developer VPS users. A lot of the pain here is not “Hermes is broken” so much as Docker + Telegram + remote dashboard + model defaults needing a production-safe path.

West Work Studios helps with this class of Hermes/OpenClaw setup. If you are actively looking for paid help rather than just reporting feedback, I’d scope it as a fixed setup/hardening pass:

- working Hetzner/Ubuntu Docker Compose path with stable container names;
- Telegram token/chat-id verification with redaction-safe commands;
- dashboard exposure guidance with security notes;
- model/fallback sanity checks;
- a copy-paste German/English runbook for reboot/restart/debug.

Do you want someone to implement and document that setup for your VPS, and is there budget for a paid fixed-scope job?
